-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, three power armors (printed 72-77 and 80-82): Cougar, Coyote, Delilah
-- 3 vehicle rows, with 35 locations and 14 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~301-northern-gun-2-power-armor-b.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x114-cougar', 'Cougar Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum (printed as 80 mph), tiring the pilot at 25% of the normal rate (10% at 35 mph/56 km or less). Climbing: 20 mph (32 km) up or down a sheer face, up to 35 mph (56 km) on 50-90 degree slopes, and full speed on all fours below 40 degrees. Leaping: 12 ft (3.7 m) up or across unassisted, 22 ft (6.7 m) with the leg thrusters; +50% with a running start for either. No power jumping travel.', 'Not possible; the leg thrusters cannot hover or fly.', 'Swims on the surface or submerged, or walks the bottom, at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots). Maximum depth 800 ft (244 m).', 'Man-sized, to the buyer''s order: height 6 to 7.6 ft (1.8 to 2.3 m); width 2.4 to 3 ft (0.73 to 0.9 m); length 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m)', '434 lbs (195.3 kg)', 250, 1, NULL, 879000, '1.8 million credits nuclear, 1.2 million Solid Oxide, 879,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. Silver-plating the Vibro-Blades is typically 22,000-30,000 credits at Northern Gun in Michigan, two to four times that nearer vampire-held Mexico. The forearm flamethrower is priced on its own at 50,000 credits as a modular alternative (gear row ng-x114-cougar-forearm-flamethrower).', 'Model Type: NG-X114. Class: Urban Assault and Xiticix Fighter Power Armor. Its designers called the prototype Bug Hunter 02, and it was paired from the start with the Lynx. Made for going into Xiticix hives: clawed fingers and toes let it scale the vertical shafts and grip walls, thruster-boosted leaps carry it up to bugs in the air, and its plating is among the heaviest NG puts on a suit. The same traits suit urban assault, SWAT and rescue teams, prison breaks, commando raids, canyon and mountain country, and boarding ships; with silver-plated blades and a slug thrower in place of the shoulder laser it becomes a vampire hunter. It is built to fight hands-free: the clawed hands grip guns poorly (-2 to strike with any handheld weapon, even big cyborg or power armor guns) and are -20% on skills needing a fine touch, such as Demolitions, Computer Operation and Palming. Every built-in energy weapon runs off the suit''s power supply. Cat-like landings: drops up to 300 ft (91.4 m) are no trouble; from 300 to 700 ft (213 m) roll 1D20, and on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions; higher drops do 3D4x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the pilot and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Bonuses: +2 to parry, +1 on initiative, +1 to roll with impact, +5% to Climbing. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: only the backpack, belts and pouches. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold too. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), blunt attacks: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks); claw strikes and kicks are weapon 6. Sensors beyond the NG standard: helmet and shoulder-gun cameras (96 hours of video, 4,000 stills), a helmet loudspeaker with a language translator and a 20-setting voice modulator, and nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m). The M.D.C. list puts the flamethrower on the left forearm, while the weapon text says the twin Vibro-Swords usually go on the left; the buyer chooses.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.72-76'),
  ('ng-x32-coyote', 'Coyote Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 34 mph (54.4 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 ft (3 m) high and 16 ft (4.9 m) across.', 'None without a jet pack or a Silent Shadow style glider, each listed as an extra cost; the sensors section names the Wild Coyote Jet Pack (80 mph/128 km, 900 ft/274 m ceiling) as standard.', 'Not built for water; swims or walks the bottom at 3 mph (4.8 km/2.6 knots), 30% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Man-size: height generally 5.6 to 7.6 ft (1.7 to 2.3 m); width 2 to 3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m); length 2 to 3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m) with jet pack or backpack', '142 lbs (64 kg)', 120, 1, NULL, 732000, '989,000 credits nuclear or 732,000 Solid Oxide, selling about equally; the lowest is stored. The Deathmark rifle comes with the armor (gear row ng-x132-deathmark-dual-sniper-rifle carries its secondary-market price).', 'Model Type: NG-X32. Class: Light Special Operations Power Armor. Begun as a pilot''s lightweight exoskeleton, it has every standard power armor system but not the usual heavy plating, so it sits between environmental body armor and power armor. Pilots of aircraft, tanks and robots like it, and so do special forces, spies, thieves, assassins, raiders and pirates: it is slim enough to wear under oversized fatigues, a jumpsuit or a long coat, letting the wearer pass for an ordinary soldier or worker, and even uncovered it is often taken for body armor. Mountings on the back take its standard hard-shell environmental backpack or most makers'' jet packs (NG, Wilk''s, Triax), popular for hit-and-run raids and quick escapes. Robot P.S. 22. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear standard, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide sold too. Any other handheld weapon (sidearm, Vibro-Blade, shotgun, backup gun) can ride on a belt or two or in a bag. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): restrained punch printed as 6D6 M.D. (more than the normal punch, so likely a misprint), normal punch 1D4 M.D., power punch 2D4 (two attacks), kick 1D6, leap kick 2D6 (two attacks). Sensors beyond the NG standard: a language translator (nine languages of the Americas plus room for 12; 98.7% accurate with a three second delay for one speaker, 78% and six seconds for three), nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m), and two telescopic helmet cameras (2 miles/3.2 km; 100 hours of video, 4,000 stills). Any NG jet pack and most competitors'' fit it. The sensors section names the Wild Coyote Jet Pack as standard (gear row ng-wild-coyote-jet-pack), while the speed section and the M.D.C. list treat a jet pack as an extra-cost swap for the backpack.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.76-77'),
  ('ng-x11-delilah', 'Delilah (and Del) Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate at high speed, 10% at 70 mph (112 km) or less. Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) high or across unassisted; jet-assisted up to 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across; +30% with a running start for either. Not flight.', 'None. At the top of a leap it can hold a hover for one melee round (15 seconds) before drifting down, and the thrusters cushion its landings.', 'Not built for water; swims 20 mph (32 km/17.3 knots) or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots). Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Height 9 ft 6 in (2.9 m); width 4 ft (1.2 m); length 4 ft (1.2 m)', '540 lbs (243 kg)', 270, 1, NULL, 825000, '1.5 million credits nuclear, 1.1 million Solid Oxide, 825,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. Cosmetic additions run 50-200 credits and custom paint 1,000-6,000.', 'Model Type: NG-X11. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit with Xiticix-fighting capabilities. Northern Gun''s companion to the Samson (NG-X9). First planned as a suit for women only, it is sold in two styles with identical stats, weapons and sensors: the curvy Delilah, often dressed up with synthetic hair, tassels, rhinestones or custom paint, and the male Del, with a Triax-style cyclopean helmet and a plainer body. The Delilah model is 62% of sales, bought by women, and women also buy about a quarter of the Dels. Like the Samson it is a tall, heavily armored all-round infantry suit with fast running and jump jets, used on the front line and in support, fast response, commando raids, recon, guard and escort duty, boarding and amphibious work, and Xiticix hive raids. Cat-like landings: its thrusters let it drop up to 300 ft (91.4 m) unharmed (half that once the back thruster unit is destroyed); from 300 to 600 ft (183 m) roll 1D20, and on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points to the pilot and stun her 1D4 melee rounds. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold. Its hands can use the large weapons built for big power armor, robots and Combat Cyborgs (man-sized guns are too small), carried in hand, on a strap or in a bag, with an oversized sidearm such as a Vibro-Sword in a belt scabbard. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors: the power armor standard only. The M.D.C. list calls the plasma weapons shoulder pulse ejectors, while the weapon text mounts them on the forearms above the blades.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.80-82');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicle_locations (vehicle_slug, location, mdc, mdc_note, ordinal) VALUES
